# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# EmailJS configuration (Vite environment variables)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the four values below, then
# restart the dev server (`npm run dev`). All four values are safe to
# expose to the browser — never put SMTP passwords or secret keys here.
#
# Where to find each value in the EmailJS dashboard
# (https://dashboard.emailjs.com):
#
#   VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY
#       "Account" tab -> "Public Key" (older accounts: "API Keys" -> "Public Key")
#
#   VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID
#       "Email Services" tab -> your email service
#       The ID looks like: service_abcdef123
#
#   VITE_EMAILJS_CONTACT_TEMPLATE_ID
#       "Email Templates" tab -> your contact-notification template
#       The ID looks like: template_uvwxyz456
#
#   VITE_EMAILJS_REPLY_TEMPLATE_ID
#       "Email Templates" tab -> your visitor auto-reply template
#       The ID looks like: template_uvwxyz456
#
# Setup steps:
#   1. Create a free account at https://dashboard.emailjs.com
#   2. Add an Email Service (Gmail / Outlook / SMTP / ...) and copy its
#      Service ID.
#   3. Create a "Contact notification" template with the variables
#      {{from_name}}, {{from_email}}, {{subject}} and {{message}}, and
#      copy its Template ID into VITE_EMAILJS_CONTACT_TEMPLATE_ID.
#      (Optionally bind the template's "Reply To" to {{reply_to}} so
#      replies from your inbox reach the sender.)
#   4. Create an "Auto-reply" template with the variables {{from_name}}
#      and {{from_email}}, and copy its Template ID into
#      VITE_EMAILJS_REPLY_TEMPLATE_ID.
#   5. Paste the four values into `.env` and restart the dev server.
#
# Vite exposes every variable prefixed with VITE_ to client code, so these
# values are visible in the browser bundle by design.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=
VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_CONTACT_TEMPLATE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_REPLY_TEMPLATE_ID=
